From 90eaaba124f50a8ef981b0cf10342c8606b24fb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:09:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] freebsd: accept capability names; resolve Linux instances
 of digest-pinned images

Two fixes for unmodified Linux manifests on FreeBSD nodes (seen with
ingress-nginx):

- getOCICapabilitiesList returned no capabilities on FreeBSD, so any
  securityContext.capabilities.add (e.g. NET_BIND_SERVICE) failed with
  "unknown capability ... to add". Return the known Linux capability
  names. Jails do not enforce them (FreeBSD has no capabilities); binding
  ports below 1024 as non-root is provided per pod through the
  net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start sysctl, which ocijail maps to the pod
  vnet's net.inet.ip.portrange.reservedhigh.

- An image referenced by tag@digest where the digest names a multi-platform
  index was resolved in local storage for the host OS. For the Linux
  RuntimeClass the stored instance is linux, so ImageStatus and
  CreateContainer failed with "no image found in image index for
  architecture arm64, variant "", OS freebsd" although the image had been
  pulled. Resolve through imageStatusByName, which retries with the
  platform's fallback OSes (linux on FreeBSD) on exactly that error.
---
